{
  "raw": {
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1335054": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Math",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Math. Mount Mercy University. St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University | Adjunct Instructor - Math St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University invite applications for an adjunct faculty pool to teach undergraduate mathematics, statistics, and related courses at our Davenport and Cedar Rapids, Iowa campuses. We are seeking qualified professionals and educators interested in teaching during Spring 2027 and future fall, spring, and summer semesters. Applicants with expertise in mathematics, statistics, applied mathematics, data science, or related fields are encouraged to apply. All positions require in-person instruction. Candidates may indicate their availability for one or both campuses and the courses they are qualified and interested in teaching. Current Spring 2027 Teaching Opportunities Mount Mercy University, Cedar Rapids, Iowa MATH-171: Elementary Functions Additional teaching opportunities at either university may become available based on enrollment, scheduling, and departmental needs. Mathematics Adjunct Pool In addition to the current vacancies, we welcome applications from candidates qualified to teach courses in the following areas: Introductory and college-level mathematics College algebra and precalculus Calculus and differential equations Probability and statistics Linear algebra and discrete mathematics Applied mathematics Data science and related quantitative disciplines Applicants do not need to be qualified or available to teach every subject listed. Course assignments will depend on institutional needs and individual qualifications. Qualifications A master's degree or higher in mathematics, statistics, applied mathematics, data science, or a closely related discipline is preferred. Candidates with appropriate graduate-level academic preparation in the subject they would teach are also encouraged to apply. Previous college-level teaching experience is preferred but not required. Relevant professional experience and demonstrated subject-matter expertise will also be considered. Applicants must be available to teach in person at the St. Ambrose University campus in Davenport, Iowa, or the Mount Mercy University campus in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. Application Interested applicants should submit a current curriculum vitae or résumé and a brief cover letter describing their academic background, relevant professional or teaching experience, and areas of instructional expertise. Applicants should indicate their preferred campus or campuses, the courses or subject areas they are qualified to teach, and their availability for Spring 2027 or future semesters. Applications will be reviewed as teaching needs arise. Inclusion in the adjunct faculty pool does not guarantee a teaching assignment. Our Mission St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses, including Mount Mercy University, are an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners. Together, we empower all members of our community to act courageously, seek wisdom through faith and reason, work for justice and mercy, and lead lives of service. St. Ambrose University and its affiliated institutions are equal opportunity employers. #HEJ"
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1327232": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer. Mount Mercy University. Public Safety Officer Mount Mercy University is seeking a dedicated and service-oriented Public Safety Officer to join our Public Safety team. This position plays a vital role in maintaining a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Public Safety Officers work a non-standard schedule and assist in providing 24/7 campus safety coverage. This position would cover hours from 4 PM to Midnight, Saturday through Wednesday. The starting pay is $16.50 an hour. The ideal candidate is a collaborative professional who demonstrates sound judgment, strong interpersonal skills, and a commitment to serving a diverse university community. Key Responsibilities Patrol campus buildings, parking lots, and grounds to help ensure the safety and security of people and property. Enforce campus security and parking policies, including building access and key control procedures. Respond to emergencies, provide assistance to injured individuals, and coordinate with local emergency responders when necessary. Conduct investigations, complete incident reports, and maintain security records. Monitor security and life-safety systems, including fire, intrusion, and access control systems. Perform routine inspections of campus safety equipment and security measures. Provide security escorts, support campus events, and collaborate with departments on safety initiatives and emergency preparedness. Participate in safety training, emergency drills, and other professional development activities. Deliver excellent customer service while maintaining a visible, approachable presence on campus. Qualifications Required High school diploma or equivalent. Valid driver's license. First Aid and CPR certification (or ability to obtain upon hire). Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and other non-traditional hours as needed. Preferred Associate degree. Previous experience in campus safety, security, law enforcement, military service, emergency response, or related field. Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Commitment to the mission and values of a faith-based university. Strong communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Ability to exercise sound judgment, de-escalate conflicts, and respond effectively in emergencies. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to maintain confidentiality. Proficiency with technology and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Benefits Competitive salary commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, and retirement plans. Generous paid time off and holidays. Tuition Remission. Professional development opportunities. Supportive and collaborative work environment. Access to campus amenities, cultural events, and recreational facilities. St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses, including Mount Mercy University in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, are an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners. Together, we empower all members of our community to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice and mercy, and to lead lives of service. St. Ambrose University and its affiliated institutions within its Catholic higher education network are equal opportunity employers. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit your resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references through our online application portal at https://stambroseuniv.applicantlist.com . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. St. Ambrose is an equal opportunity employer. #HEJ"
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1337706": {
      "title": "Student Account Representative",
      "description": "Student Account Representative. Mount Mercy University. Student Account Representative The Mount Mercy Campus of St. Ambrose University seeks a strategic and detail-oriented Student Account Representative to join the student financial services and business office teams. This role is responsible for all areas of student receivables including billing, collections & student communication at the Mount Mercy Campus. Key Responsibilities • Responsible for all student account billing & collection activities. • Respond to student account inquiries while working closely with other student services offices to investigate, analyze and provide resolutions. • Responsible for processing student refund payments • Prepare, review and distribute accurate monthly student statements for current & former students. • Responsible for timely posting of financial aid disbursements. • Responsible for adjusting student accounts for enrollment changes, fines, on campus housing, etc. in a timely manner. • Responsible for processing third party vouchers and invoicing • Prepare, review and distribute annual Form 1098T. • Responsible for the set up and monitoring of the student payment plan system with third party payment processor. Qualifications • Bachelor's degree in accounting, business, finance, or related field required. • Minimum of three years of relevant professional experience may be considered in lieu of degree. • Experience in higher education, financial operations, financial aid or student accounts preferred. Skills & Competencies • Personal computer experience in word processing, spreadsheets and database programs as well as data entry skills. • Interact ethically, professionally and confidentially with diverse groups, faculty, staff and students to develop a deep sense of trust. • Exercise professional judgment, insight, judgment, problem solving techniques, responsible decision making and independent initiative when applying policies, procedures and principles. • Demonstrated commitment to excellent customer service including the ability to effectively communicate, both orally and in writing. • Prepare and maintain records, reports and other documents with attention to detail and accuracy using a personal computer and data entry skills. • Knowledge of the operations, functions, and scope of authority of a university setting or similar environment as related to the handling and disposition of complaints, requests for information, and delegated administrative details. • Capacity to organize, manage and prioritize multiple responsibilities, deadlines, tasks and projects. • Dedication to the educational mission of a private, catholic liberal arts university. Benefits: • Competitive salary commensurate with experience. • Comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, and retirement plans. • Generous paid time off and holidays. • Tuition Remission. • Professional development opportunities. • Supportive and collaborative work environment. • Access to campus amenities, cultural events, and recreational facilities. Mission Alignment: St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses are an inclusive, Catholic and diocesan community of learners empowering all members of that community to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice and mercy, and to lead lives of service. How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit your resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references though our online application portal at https://stambroseuniv.applicantlist.com Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. EOE #HEJ"
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1340168": {
      "title": "Bachelor of Social Work Program - Tenure Track or Full-time Faculty",
      "description": "Bachelor of Social Work Program - Tenure Track or Full-time Faculty. Mount Mercy University. Bachelor of Social Work Program - Tenure Track or Full-time Faculty St. Ambrose University at the Mount Mercy campus, an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners located in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, invites applications for a Tenure Track or Full-time Professional Faculty (commensurate with experience and degree) beginning August 1, 2027. This individual will have primary teaching responsibilities in the Bachelor of Social Work Program at the Mount Mercy Campus. An engaged faculty member in this position will: Teach across the generalist social work curriculum in the BSW Program with opportunities to teach in Core Curriculum and across the School of Social Work Teach in a variety of course delivery systems, i.e., in-person, online synchronous and asynchronous, and hybrid. Serve as a Practicum Liaison for social work students Be an active advisor to students Participate and provide service on university committees Engage in scholarly activity One of eight disciplines within the College of Health and Human Services, the BSW program is located in a supportive, collaborative environment with a strong focus on teaching as well as support for scholarship. Multiple interprofessional learning events and numerous outreach services enhance the student experience. Additionally, we value self-directed community involvement, inter-professional collaboration and active professional development for faculty and staff. Program options include an in-person full-time BSW program with two locations, one on the Cedar Rapids campus and one on the Davenport campus. This position requires an MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. A tenure-track position requires a doctorate in social work or a related field. Applications from ABDs will be considered. A minimum of two years post-MSW experience is required, and evidence of effective teaching is essential. Salary will be commensurate with experience. People from under-represented populations are encouraged to apply. Priority will be given to applicants showing a strong history of teaching and practice experience with vulnerable populations. St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses, including Mount Mercy University in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, are an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners. Together, we empower all members of our community to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice and mercy, and to lead lives of service. St. Ambrose University and its affiliated institutions within its Catholic higher education network are equal opportunity employers. How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, teaching philosophy statement, vitae, and contact information for three professional references through our online application portal at https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com. Review of applications will begin November 23rd. . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. #HEJ"
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1341157": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Finance. Mount Mercy University. Finance Faculty - St. Ambrose University, Mount Mercy Campus Position Overview St. Ambrose University, an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, Assistant Professor position in finance at its Mount Mercy - Cedar Rapids, Iowa, campus. As part of a diverse community of faculty and staff representing many faith traditions and worldviews, St. Ambrose University seeks an Assistant Professor in finance who will support and advance the University's mission by teaching students, advising students , serving the university, and participating in an appropriate program of professional development. Qualifications Faculty rank (e.g., Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor) and appointment status (e.g., tenure-track or term/professional faculty) will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, experience, and institutional needs. The anticipated rank of the appointment is at the Assistant Professor level (although candidates with more extensive experience may be appointed at a higher rank). The start date is Thursday, August 12, 2027. The successful candidate will possess some combination of the following with respect to credentials and experience: For a tenure-track position, a Ph.D. in Finance is required. For a professional faculty position, a Master of Finance or MBA with a finance concentration (minimum 15 graduate credits in finance) plus five years of relevant finance experience is required. Professional certifications, such as CFA or CFP, are preferred. Teaching experience is preferred. Institutional Context In August 2024, St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University signed an agreement to fully combine the two universities. The university received approval from its accrediting body in 2025 and anticipates regulatory approval in the coming year. Mount Mercy employees became St. Ambrose employees in the summer of 2025, and the two campuses anticipate fully merging operations during the fall 2026 semester. The strategic combination of Mount Mercy and St. Ambrose University represents the proactive and innovative combination of two healthy Catholic universities. The combined university will reduce costs by significantly reducing the duplication of administrative roles across the two universities and by combining and streamlining a host of back-office operations. The combined university has also reimagined general education and academic programs with a focus on learner-centeredness, sustainability, strong student outcomes, and engaging and innovative learning experiences. St. Ambrose University was founded as a diocesan college in Davenport, Iowa in 1882. The Mount Mercy campus of St. Ambrose University was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of Mercy. St. Ambrose has a strong financial profile with an endowment of $247.5 million, of which nearly 80% is unrestricted. Collectively, St. Ambrose and Mount Mercy enroll over 3500 undergraduate and graduate students. The combined university offers more than 40 undergraduate majors and boasts a portfolio of a dozen graduate programs in a variety of fields, including multiple graduate degrees in healthcare, business, social work, education, and counseling. You can learn more about the strategic combination between St. Ambrose and Mount Mercy at https://sau.edu/education-together/ . Mission Statement St. Ambrose University is an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners that empowers all Ambrosians to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice and mercy, and to lead lives of service. Application Process Interested individuals should apply online at https://stambroseuniv.applicantlist.com and submit: Letter of application addressing: Qualifications and experience Approach to teaching and student development Interest in and capacity to contribute to the mission of St. Ambrose University Curriculum vitae or professional resume Contact information for at least three professional references Review of applications will begin at that time and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and verification of academic credentials St. Ambrose University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment."
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1341145": {
      "title": "Biology Faculty - Open Rank",
      "description": "Biology Faculty - Open Rank. Mount Mercy University. Position Overview Mt. Mercy University, a part of St. Ambrose University is an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners located in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, that invites applications for a full time, 9 month, Biology Faculty member. As part of a diverse community of faculty and staff representing many faith traditions and worldviews, St. Ambrose University seeks an open rank Biology Faculty member who will support and advance the University's mission by serving the institution across both multiple programs and the Core, with the opportunity to facilitate many community interactions and partnerships. Prior Ecologists at MMU were renowned across the state for both their expertise in the field and willingness to support community requests for support. Faculty rank and appointment status will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, experience, and institutional needs. Application Deadline: 11/30/2026 Mission Statement St. Ambrose University is an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners that empowers all Ambrosians to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice, and to lead lives of service. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Ecology, Environmental Science, or a related field (master's and ABD considered) Experience teaching biological laboratory courses at the undergraduate level Research expertise in field techniques relevant to Midwest ecosystems Position Responsibilities The individual hired for this position will be expected to enthusiastically embrace the following responsibilities and objectives : -Actively engage and advance the Catholic, diocesan mission and identity of St. Ambrose University by fostering an inclusive community of learners, integrating faith and reason, and contributing to the formation of students who act courageously, work for justice, and lead lives of service. -Teach a course load in a variety of delivery modalities. -Advise and mentor students. -Provide service to the Department, College, and University. -Be a learner-centered educator who has relevant experience with biology and ecosystems. -Embrace both the challenges and rewards of working to build a vibrant and sustainable learner-centered model for Catholic higher education across the campuses of Mount Mercy and St. Ambrose University. -Be committed to supported and guided, evidence-based innovation in pursuit of creating impactful learning experiences for students. -Contribute to the learning and professional outcomes of students across the university generally as well as in the biology program. -Engage in ongoing professional development appropriate to the faculty member's discipline, status, and academic responsibilities. -Offer high-quality learning experiences for students in a range of modalities (e.g., face-to-face, hybrid, and online) or demonstrate a willingness to learn how to do so. Teaching & Program Expectations Areas of teaching may include: Introductory and Upper-level biology courses, serving Biology programs, allied health sciences and Core Curriculum Opportunities to engage students in research, clinical practice, or applied learning Willingness to teach across modalities and contribute to innovative learning environments Institutional Context In August 2024, St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University signed an agreement to fully combine the two universities. The university received approval from its accrediting body in 2025 and anticipates regulatory approval in the coming year. Mount Mercy employees became St. Ambrose employees in the summer of 2025, and the two campuses anticipate fully merging operations during the fall 2026 semester. The strategic combination of Mount Mercy and St. Ambrose University represents the proactive and innovative combination of two healthy Catholic universities. The combined university will reduce costs by significantly reducing the duplication of administrative roles across the two universities and by combining and streamlining a host of back-office operations. The combined university has also reimagined general education and academic programs with a focus on learner-centeredness, sustainability, strong student outcomes, and engaging and innovative learning experiences. St. Ambrose University was founded as a diocesan college in Davenport, Iowa in 1882. The Mount Mercy campus of St. Ambrose University was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of Mercy. St. Ambrose has a strong financial profile with an endowment of $247.5 million, of which nearly 80% is unrestricted. Collectively, St. Ambrose and Mount Mercy enroll over 3500 undergraduate and graduate students. The combined university offers more than 40 undergraduate majors and boasts a portfolio of a dozen graduate programs in a variety of fields, including multiple graduate degrees in healthcare, business, social work, education, and counseling. You can learn more about the strategic combination between St. Ambrose and Mount Mercy at https://sau.edu/education-together/ Application Process Interested individuals should apply online and submit : Letter of application addressing: Qualifications and experience Approach to teaching and student development Curriculum vitae or professional resume Contact information for at least three professional references To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by November 30th, 2026. Review of applications will begin at that time and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and verification of academic credentials St. Ambrose University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment #HEJ"
    },
    "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1341489": {
      "title": "Ground Staff Employee",
      "description": "Ground Staff Employee. Mount Mercy University. Grounds Staff Employee - Mount Mercy University Mount Mercy University is seeking a dedicated and skilled grounds staff employee that can perform grounds tasks around our campus. As a vital part of our Grounds Team, you'll be responsible for maintaining the lawns, roads, parking lots, and campus building exteriors all around this beautiful campus. This position operates trucks, tractors, and mowers to ensure the campus exterior is safe, clean, and maintained 12 months per year. This position reports to the University's Grounds Lead and the Athletic Fields and Grounds Supervisor. This position is also needed to assist in any part of campus indoors or outdoors as needed. This role is ideal for someone who takes pride in their work, enjoys solving problems, and thrives in a supportive and professional environment. Key Responsibilities: • Maintain a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for students, staff, and visitors. • Responsible for completing work orders assigned by the management team. • Conduct regular inspections and audits to ensure compliance and identify improvement opportunities. • Prepare outdoor spaces for events, classes, and special activities. • Oversee emergency response and cleanup for incidents (e.g., leaks, spills, damage). • Maintain accurate records for work performed, including inventory and equipment reports. • Lift/move up to 50 lbs independently; heavier lifting with assistance. • Work may involve standing, walking, crawling, stooping, and other physical activity. • Promote a culture of safety among staff and volunteers, ensure OSHA guidelines and policies are followed. • Pick up trash as you come across it on the grounds of Mount Mercy's Campus • Repair and maintain the areas assigned to you • Address concerns, ensure customer satisfaction, and maintain strong relationships with campus partners. • Knowledge of grounds operations, mowing, landscaping and snow removal. • Ability to prioritize tasks and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. • Ability to work with a diverse group of individuals to achieve a common goal • Commitment to quality, safety, and service excellence. Qualifications: • High School Diploma preferred. • Landscaping, mowing or snow removal experience of 2-3 plus years • Ability to utilize and maintain various mowers, small tractors (Kubota's) and pickup trucks • Physically capable of performing all essential job functions. • Strong communication and teamwork skills. • Willingness to be on-call and occasionally work evenings or weekends. Benefits: • Competitive salary • Comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, and retirement plans. • Generous paid time off and holidays. • Tuition Remission. • Professional development opportunities. • Supportive and collaborative work environment. • Access to campus amenities, cultural events, and recreational facilities. At St. Ambrose University and the Mount Mercy campus we are more than an institution of higher learning; we are a beacon for those seeking to impact the world significantly. Guided by our foundation beliefs and values, our mission and vision reflect our dedication to fostering an inclusive, ethical, and dynamic learning environment. How to Apply : Interested candidates should submit your resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references though our online application portal at https://stambroseuniv.applicantlist.com. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. EOE #HEJ"
    }
  },
